        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d65fd2d4-17dc-5b4e-8c60-30a22a6dd120",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Tristan und Isolde, Ariane et Barbe-bleue, The Magic Flute, Faust, Aida, Don Carlos, Boris Godunov\n- People: Richard Wagner, Gottfried von Strassburg, Maurice Maeterlinck, Charles Perrault, Jerome Hines\n- Roles: Sarastro, Mephistopheles, Ramfis, Grand Inquisitor, King Mark\n- Topics: Opera librettos, source adaptations, stage presence\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Wagner composed Tristan und Isolde as a three-act opera or music drama and wrote its German libretto.\n- Tristan und Isolde was based largely on the romance by Gottfried von Strassburg.\n- The French libretto of Ariane et Barbe-bleue was adapted with very few changes from the symbolist play of the same name by Maurice Maeterlinck.\n- Maurice Maeterlinck's play Ariane et Barbe-bleue was itself loosely based on Charles Perrault's French literary tale La Barbe bleue.\n- Jerome Hines stood 6 feet 6 inches tall, and his stage presence and stentorian voice suited him to major bass roles.\n- Jerome Hines performed roles including Sarastro in The Magic Flute, Mephistopheles in Faust, Ramfis in Aida, the Grand Inquisitor in Don Carlos, the title role in Boris Godunov, and King Mark in Tristan und Isolde.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "101b7be8-cfeb-5c05-8a16-b484d236285d",
        "text": "Page: Tristan und Isolde. Sentence: Tristan und Isolde (\"Tristan and Isolde\", or \"Tristan and Isolda\", or \"Tristran and Ysolt\") is an opera, or music drama, in three acts by Richard Wagner to a German libretto by the composer, based largely on the romance by Gottfried von Strassburg.\nPage: Ariane et Barbe-bleue. Sentence: The French libretto is adapted (with very few changes) from the symbolist play of the same name by Maurice Maeterlinck, itself loosely based on the French literary tale \"La Barbe bleue\" by Charles Perrault.\nPage: Jerome Hines. Sentence: Standing 6'6\", his stage presence and stentorian voice made him ideal for such roles as Sarastro in \"The Magic Flute\", Mephistopheles in \"Faust\", Ramfis in \"Aida\", the Grand Inquisitor in \"Don Carlos\", the title role of \"Boris Godunov\" and King Mark in \"Tristan und Isolde\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
